  "language": "english",
  "text": "I get this one a lot, should we eat white rice or brown rice? The answer is always white rice. I used to think that brown rice was a healthier option and I used to eat only brown rice for years. Brown rice is actually higher in arsenic which is a heavy metal and it's also high in phytates and lectins which hinders the absorption of nutrients in your body. So eating brown rice in large quantities is definitely not the right way to go. I recommend getting an organic jasmine or basmati white rice, soaking it for about an hour and then rinsing it really well before cooking it which lowers the amount of arsenic in rice in general. And I would have that one to two times a week. I definitely do not recommend rice on a daily basis.",
